## Still open

The known deviations are unchanged from round 3:
- ints are bounded to ±2^53 (OverflowError beyond);
- a float `//` quotient beyond ±2^53 raises OverflowError;
- generator expressions are accepted only as the sole argument of a consuming builtin;
- error messages carry no counts;
- `print` takes no `sep`/`end` keywords;
- sets iterate in insertion order;
- dict views are list snapshots;
- `(x) = 1` is rejected;
- `**` with a non-integral exponent raises NotImplementedError;
- the UnboundLocalError message uses 3.11 wording.

